.\" pixpapers — forced-pixelation wallpapers for wayland
.\" conservative roff: single-line macros, groff-man + mandoc clean
.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt PIXPAPERS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pixpapers
.Nd forced-pixelation wallpapers for niri and other wayland compositors
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm pixpapers
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm pixpapers
stores wallpapers, pixelates them at literal block sizes
(8, 16, 32, 64, 128, or no pixelation as
.Ar normal )
and displays them on a wlr-layer-shell Background surface via a small
daemon. The CLI owns all state; the daemon is a pure renderer that
re-reads config on every apply. Pixelation is forced on everything the
tool sets, except per-wallpaper
.Ic pixel Ar normal
or the global
.Ic disable .
.Ss Concepts
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Preset
Pixel block size: 8 | 16 | 32 | 64 | 128 | normal (default 16).
.It Placement
.Ar fit
(letterbox, default),
.Ar cover-gutter
(mat border in bg color),
.Ar cover-crop ,
.Ar stretch .
.It Variants
The displayed image is a cached tiny render (kilobytes), generated lazily
from the stored original; switches never touch the original.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic add Ar path Op Fl -title Ar t
Add a wallpaper (deduplicated by content hash; re-encoded lossless-optimized).
.It Ic list
List the library.
.It Ic remove Ar id
Remove entry, original and variants.
.It Ic set Ar id
Apply now; auto-starts the daemon when WAYLAND_DISPLAY is set.
.It Ic cycle Op Ar by
Rotate the current wallpaper by
.Ar by
(default 1).
.It Ic pixel Ar id Ar preset
Per-wallpaper preset (see Concepts).
.It Ic placement Ar id Ar placement
Per-wallpaper placement.
.It Ic bg Ar id Ar color
Border/gutter color, #rrggbb.
.It Ic gutter Ar id Ar px
Gutter width for cover-gutter in output pixels.
.It Ic default pixel|placement Ar value
Change the global default for new/unset entries.
.It Ic enable No / Ic disable
Global pixelation on/off (disable renders originals only).
.It Ic status Op Fl -json Op Fl -bench
Daemon truth when running, filesystem view otherwise; --bench adds
self-timed latencies, cache hit rate, RSS and fd counts.
.It Ic export Ar id Ar WxH Op Fl -pixel Ar p Op Fl -placement Ar pl Op Fl -bg Ar c Op Fl -gutter Ar n Op Fl o Ar out
Offline render with the daemon's exact composite path.
.It Ic optimize Op Fl -all
Re-run storage optimization over the library.
.It Ic daemon
Run the daemon in the foreground (you rarely need this; mutating
commands spawn it detached).
.It Ic stop
Politely stop the running daemon (IPC).
.It Ic completions Ar shell
Print a completion script for bash, zsh or fish.
.El
.Sh EXIT CODES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
User error (unknown id, bad value, already-running daemon).
.It 2
Internal error (I/O, decode, config corruption).
.It 43
Daemon only: the compositor went away (session end / niri restart).
Surfaces, socket and pidfile were torn down. Do not restart the daemon
on 43 into the same session.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Required for rendering and auto-spawn.
.It Ev PIXPAPERS_HOME
Hermetic root replacing data+config+state directories (tests, portable setups).
.It Ev PIXPAPERS_LOG
Daemon log filter (error..trace, default info).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Pa ~/.config/pixpapers/config.toml
.Pa ~/.local/share/pixpapers/library.json
.Pa ~/.local/share/pixpapers/library/<id>/
.Pa ~/.local/state/pixpapers/sock , pid , log
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pixpapers add ~/Pictures/nebula.png
pixpapers list
pixpapers set 4a1c9f          # daemon auto-starts, wallpaper in ~90 ms
pixpapers pixel 4a1c9f 8
pixpapers bg 4a1c9f "#1a2b3c"
pixpapers export 4a1c9f 3840x2160 --pixel 32 -o /tmp/preview.png
pixpapers status --bench
.Ed
.Sh "EXIT BEHAVIOR NOTE"
A daemon exiting 43 is normal at logout; systemd units must set
RestartPreventExitStatus=43 (see contrib/pixpapers.service).
.Sh BUGS
https://github.com/lariocpt/pixelated-papers/issues
Include: compositor + version, output mode/scale,
.Ic pixpapers status
output.
